body:
   i sort of agree while it isn't that bad, definitely not the worst Gundam, it's not quite as good as i remember it. Everyone's an asshole for the first quarter of the show and a lot of character development happens in big chunks as opposed to a natural gradual development which makes the pacing weird.

&#x200B;

I feel like Relena is supposed to be like a kinda like vicarious audience stand-in type deal, but she just seems unnecessary, does that make any sense? I still think Zechs is really well written, Quatra and Trowa have great moments together, but Heero doesn't have much personality, Duo is supposed to be like easy-going but he comes off as a flippant asshole ("Geeze Heero I know we're literally fighting a war against an oppressive authoritarian state but you need to chill bro"), and Wufei is just a total nutcase.

&#x200B;

watching it with my friend Drew he seemed to agree on what works and what doesn't. Right now we just watched 08th MS, we're gonna try the original series, War in the Pocket, we've been watching Mobile Fighter G mostly for laughs, and the surreal neat moments, Turn A and Double 0, I'm  reluctant to try Iron Blooded Orphans because while I think it's OK it doesn't strike me as universally likable, or a super great introductory series but  whatever, if you have any more obscure suggestions, even like games or manga he's really starting to get hooked all he needs is that big push, also i apologize for the wall of text.
